docs {
  # Hard Delete Error By ID

  This request is used to permanently delete an error history based on the provided `ID`. However, it will also search for all errors with the same `message` and delete them. This request interacts with the MySQL database, and has a protected routes (Admin only).

  ## Path Parameters

  | Name | Type   | Required | Description | Example                               |
  |------|--------|----------|--------------|------------------------------------------|
  | id   | string | yes      | Error ID    | e1288783-a5d4-1c4c-2cd6-0e92f7cc3bf9   |

  ## Responses

  **200 — error permanently deleted**
```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "error permanently deleted"
  }
```

  **401 — protected route need to include sign in token as authorization bearer**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "you need to include the authorization token from login"
  }
```

  **404 — error failed to permanently deleted**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "error not found"
  }
```

  **500 — Internal Server Error**
```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "something wrong. please contact admin"
  }
```
}